    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite passes.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented soft-match (\"possible duplicate\") detection for `POST /api/owners`. When a new owner isn't a hard duplicate (which `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique` still rejects with 409) but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` while carrying a *different* telephone, the owner is still created with `possibleDuplicate: true` and `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id; otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`.\n\nFollowing the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions and mirroring the existing `AssignNamesakeCount` pattern (compute-at-creation, store, return):\n\n1. **`AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`** (new function) \u2014 after `BuildOwner` produces the entity, scans pre-existing owners for a case-insensitive `lastName` + exact `postcode` match with a differing telephone, and mutates the entity in place (`possibleDuplicate` / `possibleDuplicateOf`, lowest matching id for determinism). Skips when no postcode is supplied.\n\n2. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `assignPossibleDuplicate` step between `assignNamesakeCount` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added persisted `possibleDuplicate` (Boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (Integer) columns with getters/setters. MapStruct's `OwnerMapper` auto-maps them by name, so both the create response and `GET /api/owners/{id}` return them.\n\n4. **Schema** \u2014 added `possible_duplicate` / `possible_duplicate_of` columns to the hsqldb (test) and h2 (runtime) `owners` DDL.\n\n5. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two read-only fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them.\n\n`AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` and the full suite pass (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 the repo's only test class).",
